  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Snapshot — 25 Nov 2026",
      "items": [
        "User decisions: Spring Boot, React TypeScript, PostgreSQL; isolated practices; patient-first native app (React Native with Expo, demo-only).",
        "Built on main: web sign-in and recovery, invitation activation, practice context, patient search and registration, the read side of a record's chronology and the local demonstration; 23 of the 100 contract operations are served. Workers, files, the AI and notification adapters, documents and the native app are not built. ADR-001–007 remain proposals; ADR-008–014 are accepted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Core journey",
      "items": [
        "Record + dated sources → deterministic clinician brief → encounter → report / separate explanation → human review → explicit patient publication.",
        "The brief stays DRAFT and is acknowledged only. Validation never publishes. See the documents view for the actual gates. Only the read side of the record and its dated sources is built (story 3.2)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Every boundary stays scoped",
      "items": [
        "Current capability plus practice and record ownership on queries, mutations, jobs, sources, files and exports. Administrator does not imply clinical access.",
        "If-Match, idempotency, database overlap constraints, audit and outbox protect state changes. Provider calls run outside the originating transaction. Built so far: RLS under a non-owner runtime role, If-Match on patient edits, idempotency receipts, audit events and outbox rows; overlap constraints, workers and provider calls are planned."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Phased target, not an increment-1 inventory",
      "items": [
        "I1: web journey, seeded slots/document, deterministic adapters, P-03 PDF. I2: complete web entry/upload/scheduling/admin and P-01/P-02. I3: PWA → Android app (Expo) + push. I4: iOS demo gate and conditional release extensions. Merged so far (increment 1): stories 10.1, 10.2, 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 1.4, 3.1, 3.2 and 9.1.",
        "No required broker, Redis, microservices or vector database. Object storage and real antivirus scanning are deferred; hosting and exact dependency versions remain gated."
      ]
    }
  ]
